(footprint "SW_200_MDP3_DPDT"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "hand")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Taiway 200-MDP3-T2B1M2QE sub-miniature DPDT ON-OFF-ON toggle, PCB vertical. M2 PC thru-hole terminals on a 2.54 x 5.08 grid, 10-48 UNS bushing (o4.80 thread, 5.50 high, flat) -> o4.95 panel hole. Body 8.10 (throw axis, X) x 9.10. PAD 1 and PAD 4 ARE THE CENTRE PINS = the switch's commons. This is a DELIBERATE remap of the datasheet's numbering (which calls the centre terminals 2 and 5): the schematic drives the common from SW_DPDT_x2 pin 1/4 (A), so pad 1/4 must be the centre for the common net to land on the common terminal. SW_DPDT_x2 draws its blade pivoting at pin B, but that is cosmetic -- KiCad does not model switch internals in a netlist, only pin->pad->terminal. Do not 'correct' this to datasheet numbering without also rewiring every switch in the schematic.")
	(tags "toggle switch dpdt on-off-on subminiature taiway 200 eurorack")
